An indulgent, cozy potato soup topped like a loaded baked potato. Yukon Gold potatoes are simmered in chicken broth and blended with sour cream and sharp cheddar, then topped with golden, cheese-baked Tater Tots and crispy bacon.

*Adapted from [Food Network Kitchen](https://www.foodnetwork.com/recipes/food-network-kitchen/cheesy-potato-soup-3894914).*

## Ingredients

- 1 pound frozen Tater Tots
- 3 cups shredded sharp cheddar cheese (about 12 ounces, divided)
- 2 tablespoons unsalted butter
- 1 yellow onion, diced (about 1 ½ cups)
- Kosher salt and freshly ground black pepper, to taste
- 2 cloves garlic, minced
- 4 Yukon Gold potatoes, peeled and diced (about 1 ½ pounds)
- 4 cups low-sodium chicken broth
- ¾ cup water (plus up to ¼ cup extra for thinning)
- 2 slices thick-cut bacon, diced
- ½ cup sour cream, divided
- 2 tablespoons chopped fresh chives

## Instructions

1. **Bake the Cheesy Tot Crunchies:** Heat your oven to 425°F (220°C). Scatter the frozen Tater Tots evenly across a rimmed sheet pan. Bake for 20 minutes, flipping them halfway through with a spatula so all sides become deeply golden and crisp. Dust 1 cup of the shredded cheddar over the tots and return to the oven for 5 minutes until the cheese is bubbling and melted onto the tots. Keep warm.
2. **Sauté the Aromatics:** While the tots roast, melt 2 tablespoons butter in a Dutch oven or stockpot over medium heat. Stir in the chopped onion along with ¼ teaspoon kosher salt and black pepper. Sauté for about 5 minutes until soft and translucent. Stir in the minced garlic and cook for 1 minute until fragrant.
3. **Boil the Potatoes:** Tip the diced Yukon Gold potatoes into the pot, followed by the chicken broth, ¾ cup water, and ½ teaspoon salt. Crank heat to high to bring the liquid to a rolling boil, then dial down the flame to a gentle simmer. Cover with a lid and cook for 10 to 12 minutes until the potato chunks are tender when pierced with a fork.
4. **Crisp the Bacon:** In a small frypan over medium-high heat, cook the diced bacon for about 5 minutes until browned and crispy. Transfer with a slotted spoon to a paper towel-lined saucer.
5. **Puree and Melt the Cheeses:** Turn off the heat and blend the soup directly in the pot using an immersion stick blender until completely silky and smooth. If you desire a slightly looser consistency, whisk in up to ¼ cup additional water. Stir in ¼ cup of sour cream and the remaining 2 cups of shredded cheddar. Place over low heat, stirring continuously until the cheese melts into a rich, creamy soup.
6. **Ladle and Load:** Ladle hot potato soup into deep serving bowls. Crown each bowl with a mound of the cheesy crisp Tater Tots, a sprinkle of smoky bacon bits, a spoonful of sour cream, and chopped fresh chives. Finish with freshly cracked pepper.

## Notes

- **Potato Choice:** Yukon Golds produce an exceptionally buttery, creamy texture naturally without needing heavy cream.
- **Tot Crunch:** Keep the cheesy Tater Tots on the baking sheet until right before serving so they stay maximally crunchy when placed on the soup.
